Hello Marcel,

Thank you for the quick reply.

I know that Broadcom does not release these files officially.

Just to clarify: When extracting the firmware file from the publicly released Windows driver, the file that works is actually called "4356a2rtecdc.bin" (driver obtained from my vendor's site: https://www.wortmann.de/de-de/systeminformation/R5105360.aspx - in German; look for the item "Terra Mobile 360-11 Bluetooth Treiber").

When talking about file names, I do not refer to the Broadcom names, but rather to the canonical names used by the linux kernel. These are the same names as used by this upstream repository https://github.com/winterheart/broadcom-bt-firmware/ and the actual files present on my system (from the Debian package "firmware-brcm80211" - https://packages.debian.org/buster/firmware-brcm80211 ).

All I am saying is that for the particular device present in my machine (pci id 14e4:43ec), the firmware file "BCM4354A2-13d3-3485.hcd" is requested (which does not exist in the Debian package "firmware-brcm80211"), but the device actually works just fine with "BCM4356A2-13d3-3485.hcd" (which is present in the Debian package).
This, along with the fact that the device is identified as "BCM4356" by lspci, made me think that this could be a typo in the kernel source. Actually winterheart, the maintainer of the above-mentioned firmware repository, thinks the same.

That being said, please find attached the output of btmon (btmon.txt contains the output on the console, trace.log is the actual trace).

Please let me know if you need anything else.

Best regards,
Ferdinand

